# coder-fork @VERSION@ – install

Coder @CODER_VERSION@ (the fork) for an air-gapped Kubernetes cluster. This folder holds only what runs Coder from
the fork: the images of ours the chart runs and the chart, `coder-airgapped-@VERSION@.tgz`, which installs the whole
platform with one `helm install`.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `coder-airgapped-@VERSION@.tgz` | The chart |
| `<name>_<tag>.tar.gz` | @IMAGE_COUNT@ images of ours, `docker save` + gzip (@IMAGES_SIZE@); one over 1900 MiB is split into `<file>.part-00`, `-01`, ... (`cat` joins them) |
| `push-images.sh` | Checks the files, then loads each image and pushes it to your registry (docker only) |
| `IMAGES.txt` | Each image: its reference, file(s), size, config and manifest digests |
| `values-eks-airgap.example.yaml` | The values to start `my-values.yaml` from |
| `values-ha.example.yaml` | High availability, on top of your values |
| `gateway-api-v1.6.0-standard-install.yaml`, `traefik-41.4.0.tgz`, `traefik-41.4.0.reference-values.yaml`, `traefik-41.4.0.ha-values.yaml`, `cloudnative-pg-0.29.0.tgz` | The prerequisites (step 0) |
| `SHA256SUMS` | Every file here (`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`); `SHA256SUMS.joined`: the split archives, joined |
| `CVE-REPORT.md` | The release's CVE scan (when it was built with one) |

## Before you start

The cluster needs these already:

- **Kubernetes 1.27 or newer with amd64 (x86_64) nodes** – the images are amd64 only.
- **DNS** for `coder.<your-domain>` and `*.<your-domain>` – from your users' machines **and from inside the
  cluster**: workspace agents and the chart's Jobs (the first user, the template pushes) reach Coder at
  `https://coder.<your-domain>`, and without it they fail quietly. A cluster with no such DNS (minikube, kind) can
  have CoreDNS answer it with the Gateway: in `kubectl -n kube-system edit configmap coredns`, add to the `.:53`
  block `rewrite name regex (.*)\.<your-domain> traefik.traefik.svc.cluster.local answer auto` (the domain's dots
  escaped), then `kubectl -n kube-system rollout restart deploy/coredns`.
- **Your certificate:** `ca.crt` (the CA that signed it) and `wildcard.crt` / `wildcard.key` for `*.<your-domain>`.
- **A container registry** (ECR, Harbor, ...) – `$REGISTRY` below, the chart's `global.registry` – that already holds
  the **public images** the chart runs, under the same paths (the source host left out). This release carries none
  of them (nor the prerequisites' two images, step 0). No registry - a single minikube node without internet? Load every image into the node instead (`docker
  load`, then `minikube image load`): ours from this folder, the public ones saved on a connected machine by the
  digests below, plus the prerequisites' (`ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg:1.30.0`, `docker.io/traefik:v3.7.12`),
  and set `global.registry: ""`.

| In your registry | Pull it on a connected machine as (tested digest) |
|---|---|
@PUBLIC_IMAGES@

High availability (`values-ha.example.yaml`: the database's synchronous standby and PgBouncer pooler, and more
replicas) also runs:

| In your registry | Pull it on a connected machine as (tested digest) |
|---|---|
@PUBLIC_IMAGES_HA@

Files: `ca.crt` (the CA that signed your HTTPS certificate), `wildcard.crt` / `wildcard.key` (the certificate for
`*.<your-domain>`), and for OIDC sign-in (Keycloak) `keycloak-ca.crt` and the client secret.
Tools: `docker`, `helm`, `kubectl` (and `aws` for ECR).

## 0. The prerequisites (this folder carries them)

```bash
kubectl apply --server-side -f gateway-api-v1.6.0-standard-install.yaml          # Gateway API CRDs v1.6.0
kubectl create namespace traefik
kubectl -n traefik create secret tls coder-airgapped-tls --cert=wildcard.crt --key=wildcard.key
helm upgrade --install traefik traefik-41.4.0.tgz -n traefik --wait \
  -f traefik-41.4.0.reference-values.yaml \
  --set image.registry=$REGISTRY                   # its image from your registry ($REGISTRY/traefik:v3.7.12)
helm upgrade --install cnpg cloudnative-pg-0.29.0.tgz -n cnpg-system --create-namespace --wait \
  --set image.repository=$REGISTRY/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg --set image.tag=1.30.0
```

Traefik's reference values carry the Gateway `traefik/traefik-gateway` (HTTPS with the `coder-airgapped-tls`
Secret); it is stock Traefik (nothing rewrites a response). For high availability add
`-f traefik-41.4.0.ha-values.yaml`. Skip any of these the cluster already has. Tested: @TRAEFIK@, CloudNativePG
@CNPG@.

## 1. Push the images

```bash
docker login $REGISTRY       # ECR: aws ecr get-login-password | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin $REGISTRY
./push-images.sh $REGISTRY   # --dry-run first if you like; ECR=1 ./push-images.sh $REGISTRY creates the ECR repositories
```

It checks every file against `SHA256SUMS` first, then loads, tags and pushes each image as
`$REGISTRY/user187x/<name>:<tag>`, and ends with a summary.

## 2. Values

```bash
cp values-eks-airgap.example.yaml my-values.yaml    # change every CHANGE-ME (global.registry: $REGISTRY, the domain, ...)
```

Kubelets with self-signed serving certificates (minikube, kind, kubeadm's defaults) need
`metricsServer: {kubeletInsecureTLS: true}`, else metrics-server cannot read them. For high availability pass
`-f values-ha.example.yaml` after your values (one Coder serves, a standby takes over; the database's synchronous
standby and pooler).

## 3. Install

```bash
helm install coder coder-airgapped-@VERSION@.tgz -n coder --create-namespace -f my-values.yaml \
  --set secrets.tlsCa.create=true --set-file secrets.tlsCa.caCrt=ca.crt \
  --set secrets.wildcardTls.create=true \
  --set-file secrets.wildcardTls.tlsCrt=wildcard.crt --set-file secrets.wildcardTls.tlsKey=wildcard.key \
  --wait --timeout 20m
```

The namespace must be `coder` (the workspace template accepts no other). With OIDC sign-in (Keycloak), add these
two lines; `client-secret.txt` holds the client secret with no trailing newline
(`tr -d '\r\n' <secret.txt >client-secret.txt`):

```bash
  --set secrets.oidcCa.create=true --set-file secrets.oidcCa.caCrt=keycloak-ca.crt \
  --set secrets.oidcClient.create=true --set-file secrets.oidcClient.clientSecret=client-secret.txt \
```

## 4. Sign in

Open `https://coder.<your-domain>` and sign in as **`admin@admin.com`** / **`admin`** – then change the password at
once (your avatar › Account › Security).

The image builder (Templates › Images) builds on the workspace image in your registry: nothing more to set up.
The dashboard's default logo and avatar (which the source repository's `install.sh` makes from its `defaults/`) are
optional: without them it shows Coder's, and an admin sets the platform's in Admin Settings › Appearance (the image
store offers the platform's logo, `minecraft-cube.gif`).

The next release: push its images, then `helm upgrade coder coder-airgapped-<next>.tgz -n coder` with the same options.
